Arthur,<br />
<br />
This confirms yesterday's call, and the attached signed letter puts it on T=
orvane letterhead so there is no ambiguity in either of our files.<br />
<br />
Prescott Vane's engagement under Matter 2011-0284 is limited to Torvane's c=
laims against Ridgeline Constructors, Inc. arising out of the Kelling Stati=
on Unit 2 expansion. Torvane has considered the potential warranty claim ag=
ainst Brandt Thermal Systems, Inc. relating to the Unit 2 regenerative ther=
mal oxidizer, and has elected not to assert it, for the commercial reasons =
we discussed. That claim is expressly outside the scope of your engagement,=
 and Prescott Vane is not asked to take any step to evaluate, preserve, or =
pursue it - including any tolling agreement, notice, or protective filing.<=
br />
<br />
Your firm advised us, orally and in writing, of the limitations consequence=
s of this election, including that the claim is likely to become time-barre=
d, and Torvane accepts those consequences. This confirmation is not limited=
 to any period and stands unless I withdraw it in writing.<br />
<br />
I see no need to re-paper the engagement letter; this email and the attache=
d letter are the record.<br />
<br />
Thank you for pressing the point as hard as you did. It was the right advic=
e; it is just not the road we are taking.<br />
<br />
Rosalind<br />
<br />
Rosalind Tenniel<br />
General Counsel<br />
Torvane Industrial Group, Inc.
